    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0372" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg286"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d197-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Excerpts]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d197-f2"/>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-19">19 November
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Roosevelt,
                    Personal and Top Secret number 825.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <pb facs="0373" n="287" xml:id="pg287"/>
                <p>6. Para two of your 649<anchor n="3" xml:id="d197-f3"/> causes me alarm. If after
                    Germany’s) collapse you “must bring the American troops home as rapidly as
                    transportation problems will permit” and if the French are to have no equipped
                    post-war army or time to make one, or to give it battle experience, how will it
                    be possible to hold down western Germany beyond the present Russian occupied
                    line? We certainly could not undertake the task without your aid and that of the
                    French. All would therefore rapidly disintegrate as it did last time. I hope,
                    however, that my fears are groundless. I put my faith in you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prime</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f2" n="2" xml:id="d197-f2-content">
                <p>Other portions of this telegram are printed <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg17">p. 17</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d197-f3" n="3" xml:id="d197-f3-content">
